    "title": "Missing person alert cancelled for woman in Etowah County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "UPDATE: The Missing and Endangered Person Alert for Lisa Kay Dutton has been cancelled. SOUTHSIDE, Ala. ( WIAT ) — The Alabama Law Enforcement Agency issued a missing and endangered person alert for a woman who was last seen in Southside on Wednesday. According to the ALEA, Lisa Kay Dutton, 56, was last seen around 2 p.m. in the area of Cheyenne Drive. That is by the Coosa River. She may have a condition impairing her judgment. She was last seen wearing a dark green shirt and white floral print shorts. Dutton stands at 5-foot-3 and weighs around 130 pounds. She has hazel eyes and blonde or strawberry hair. There is a butterfly tattoo on her right wrist. Those with information on Dutton’s whereabouts are asked to call the Southside Police Department at 256-442-2312 or 911. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS 42.",
